# ADT constructor type enforcement: [Error msg: 42] should produce a type warning
# because Error.msg expects String but receives Int(42).
# The [Ok value: 42] call is valid — Ok is polymorphic on `a`.
# Eval proceeds regardless of type errors (advisory).
[
  Result: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]]
  ok-val:  [Ok value: 42]
  err-bad: [Error msg: 42]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(value), "Error": Function(msg)}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Dict({"value": Int(42)})), "err-bad": Variant(Result.Error, Dict({"msg": Int(42)}))})

=== warn
[UnificationFailure] cannot unify String with 42
